  F5 CRPS, 100 sims per side, 6 salts

  1,121 hitters in both split sources; mean |exact - derived| K% = 0.0079 over 1,700 cells
  exact split spread, 241 hitters with 80+ each hand: sd 0.0305

  off (overall)     3,664 sides   CRPS 1.60237 +/- 0.00127
  derived splits    3,664 sides   CRPS 1.59609 +/- 0.00155
  EXACT in-sample   3,664 sides   CRPS 1.59554 +/- 0.00168
  EXACT 2023-25     3,664 sides   CRPS 1.60773 +/- 0.00162

  derived splits   vs off:  -0.00628 +/- 0.00203  ( -3.1 sd)   BETTER
  EXACT in-sample  vs off:  -0.00682 +/- 0.00196  ( -3.5 sd)   BETTER
  EXACT 2023-25    vs off:  +0.00537 +/- 0.00231  ( +2.3 sd)   worse

  NEGATIVE means handedness LOWERS CRPS, which is the
  improvement — `_paired_se(a, b)` returns b - a and lower loss
  is better, so the obvious reading of the sign is backwards.
  The bar every candidate is held to is 2 sd, and the salts are
  what make that number mean anything.
